  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on skewness, specifically preferring the lottery that is more right-skewed (i.e., has a higher probability assigned to unfavorable outcomes relative to favorable ones). To assess skewness, we compare the distribution of probabilities across outcomes. Lottery A offers 3000 Euros with 100% probability, so it has no variance and thus no skewness—it is a certain outcome. Lottery B offers 4000 Euros with 80% probability and 0 Euros with 20% probability. The 20% chance of 0 Euros represents an unfavorable outcome, while the 80% chance of a higher amount (4000) is favorable. Since the unfavorable outcome has lower probability (20%) compared to the favorable one (80%), Lottery B is left-skewed (not right-skewed). A right-skewed lottery would have high probability on low outcomes and low probability on high outcomes (e.g., 90% chance of 0, 10% chance of a large gain). Therefore, neither lottery is right-skewed in the typical sense, but Lottery A, being deterministic, could be considered maximally right-skewed only if one defines 'unfavorable' as any outcome below the maximum—but this is not standard. More accurately, Lottery B is left-skewed due to a small chance of a low outcome (0) and high chance of a high outcome. Thus, the reason would not prefer Lottery B on grounds of right-skewness. Instead, it would prefer a lottery with higher probability on worse outcomes. In this case, Lottery A (certain 3000) assigns 100% to an outcome that is worse than 4000 but better than 0. If we define 'favorable' as the best possible outcome (4000), then only Lottery B has any chance at a favorable outcome. But the reason prefers more right-skewness, i.e., higher probability on unfavorable outcomes. Lottery A gives 3000 for sure, which is less than 4000, so if 4000 is the only favorable outcome, then 3000 and 0 are both unfavorable—making Lottery A 100% on unfavorable, Lottery B 80% on favorable (4000) and 20% on unfavorable (0). Then Lottery A is more right-skewed (100% on unfavorable) than B (20% on unfavorable). So the reason would prefer Lottery A because it is more right-skewed under this definition. Therefore, the reason can be applied: it prefers Lottery A.",
